    summary_60s: 'Electron diffraction and de Broglie formula. Momentum and energy duality. Compton effect and Heisenberg’s uncertainty principle. Wave–Particle Duality Wave–particle duality states that: Light shows both wave properties (e.g., interference, diffraction) and particle properties (e.',
    key_formulas: '• Wave Speed Equation: v = f × λ\n• Period & Frequency: T = 1/f | f = 1/T\n• Snell\'s Law of Refraction: n = sin i / sin r = v₁ / v₂ = c / v\n• Critical Angle: sin c = 1/n\n• Lens Formula: 1/f = 1/u + 1/v | Magnification: m = v/u = h_i/h_o',
