    subtopic: 'Fluids At Rest',
    summary_60s: 'Fluids are substances that can flow and conform to the shape of their containers. They deform continuously under external forces such as pressure or gravity. Liquids : Have definite volume but no fixed shape. Gases : Have neither definite volume nor shape. The study of fluids and',
