    summary_60s: 'Change of state refers to the transformation of matter from one phase to another. Matter typically exists in one of three states: solid, liquid, or gas. A change of state occurs when heat is added or removed, causing the substance to transition between these states. The three pri',
    key_formulas: '• Newton\'s 2nd Law: F = ma = (mv - mu) / t\n• Momentum: p = m × v | Impulse: J = F × t = Δp\n• Work Done: W = F × d cos θ (Joules)\n• Kinetic Energy: KE = ½mv² | Potential Energy: PE = mgh\n• Power: P = Work / time = F × v',
